Q: Converting HH:MM time input to minutes in SurveyJS expression A: <p>There are a few ways forward.</p>
<h4>Register a Custom Function</h4>
<p>The most declarative would be to define a custom function and then register it with Surveyjs using the provided <code>FunctionFactory.Instance.register()</code>.</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>// SurveyComponent.jsx

import { FunctionFactory } from &quot;survey-core&quot;;

function getTotalMinutes(params) {
  const timeInput = params[0];
  if (
    timeInput == undefined ||
    timeInput.length &lt; 5 ||
    !timeInput.includes(&quot;:&quot;)
  )
    return 0;

  const [HH, MM] = params[0].split(&quot;:&quot;);

  return parseInt(HH, 10) * 60 + parseInt(MM, 10);
}

FunctionFactory.Instance.register(&quot;getTotalMinutes&quot;, getTotalMinutes);

function SurveyComponent() {...}
</code></pre>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>// json.js

export const json = {
  elements: [
    {
      type: &quot;text&quot;,
      name: &quot;timeInput&quot;,
      title: &quot;Enter time (HH:MM)&quot;,
      inputType: &quot;time&quot;,
      isRequired: true,
    },
    {
      type: &quot;text&quot;,
      name: &quot;totalMinutes&quot;,
      title: &quot;Total Minutes&quot;,
      visible: true,
      readOnly: true,
      defaultValueExpression: &quot;{totalMinutes}&quot;,
    },
  ],
  calculatedValues: [
    {
      name: &quot;totalMinutes&quot;,
      expression: &quot;getTotalMinutes({timeInput})&quot;,
    },
  ],
};
</code></pre>
<p>see: <a href="https://surveyjs.io/form-library/examples/use-custom-functions-in-expressions/reactjs#" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Surveyjs: Custom Functions in Expression</a></p>
<p><a href="https://codesandbox.io/p/sandbox/floral-fast-5r4qvq" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Sandbox</a></p>
<h4>Built-in Date Functions</h4>
<p>Alternatively, if you aren't able to add the javascript, you could use the built-in date functions that Surveyjs provides. This is a little hacky, but also quite tidy. It first tests using <code>notempty</code> and then simply concatenates the <code>timeInput</code> into a date string to pass to <code>dateDiff</code>.</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>iif({timeInput} notempty, dateDiff('2000-01-01T00:00:00', '2000-01-01T'+{timeInput}+':00', 'minutes'), 0)
</code></pre>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>export const json = {
  elements: [
    {
      type: &quot;text&quot;,
      name: &quot;timeInput&quot;,
      title: &quot;Enter time (HH:MM)&quot;,
      inputType: &quot;time&quot;,
      isRequired: true,
    },
    {
      type: &quot;text&quot;,
      name: &quot;totalMinutes&quot;,
      title: &quot;Total Minutes&quot;,
      visible: true,
      readOnly: true,
      defaultValueExpression:
        &quot;iif({timeInput} notempty, dateDiff('2000-01-01T00:00:00', '2000-01-01T'+{timeInput}+':00', 'minutes'), 0)&quot;,
    },
  ],
};
</code></pre>
<p>see: <a href="https://surveyjs.io/survey-creator/documentation/end-user-guide/expression-syntax" rel="nofollow noreferrer">dateDiff</a></p>
<p><a href="https://codesandbox.io/p/sandbox/surveyjs-custom-expression-forked-jn5dqy" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Sandbox</a></p>
<hr />
<p><strong>Note:</strong> Your current sandbox <em><strong>is</strong></em> throwing an error if you look in the console.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Invalid expression: 'iif({timeInput}, (Number(split({timeInput},
':')[0]) * 60) + Number(split({timeInput}, ':')[1]), 0)'.</p>
</blockquote>

Q: Extension for Array where Element is Optional A: <h3>Extension for Array where Element is Optional:</h3>
<pre><code>extension Array {

    subscript&lt;T&gt;(safe index: Index) -&gt; T? where Element == T? {
        get {
            if (indices.contains(index))
                 { return self[index] }
            else { return nil }
        }
        set {
            if      (index &lt;  self.count) { self[index] = newValue }
            else if (index == self.count) { self.append(newValue) }
            else if (index &gt;  self.count) {
                for i in self.count ... index {
                    if (i != index) { self.append(nil) }
                    if (i == index) { self.append(newValue) }
                }
            }
        }
    }

}
</code></pre>
<h3>Test:</h3>
<pre><code>func test_arraySafe() {
    var data    : [String?] = []
    var expected: [String?] = []

    data = []
    data[safe: 0] = nil
    expected = [nil]
    print(data == expected)

    data = []
    data[safe: 0] = &quot;value 1&quot;
    expected = [&quot;value 1&quot;]
    print(data == expected)

    data = []
    data[safe: 4] = &quot;value 5&quot;
    expected = [nil, nil, nil, nil, &quot;value 5&quot;]
    print(data == expected)

    data = []
    data[safe: 4] = &quot;value 5&quot;
    data[safe: 1] = &quot;value 2&quot;
    data[safe: 6] = &quot;value 7&quot;
    expected = [nil, &quot;value 2&quot;, nil, nil, &quot;value 5&quot;, nil, &quot;value 7&quot;]
    print(data == expected)

    data = []
    data[safe: 4] = &quot;value 5&quot;
    data[safe: 1] = &quot;value 2&quot;
    data[safe: 6] = &quot;value 7&quot;
    data[safe: 4] = nil
    data[safe: 6] = nil
    expected = [nil, &quot;value 2&quot;, nil, nil, nil, nil, nil]
    print(data == expected)
}
</code></pre>

Q: Google Doc add ons with multiple sidebars. Now a sidebar only displays if the doc is refreshed A: <p>Internally, Google Docs now aggressively caches UI state. When <code>showSidebar(</code>) is called while Docs <em>believes</em> the UI context is already initialized (or at least partially detached), the HTML is created, but not reattached to the DOM. Refreshing the document resets that state, which is why it suddenly appears.</p>
<pre><code>function displayFormatTableSidebar() {
  var html = HtmlService.createHtmlOutputFromFile('Launcher')
    .setWidth(1)
    .setHeight(1);
  DocumentApp.getUi().showModalDialog(html, ' ');
}

function openSidebar() {
  var ui = HtmlService.createTemplateFromFile('FTBL_Sidebar')
    .evaluate()
    .setTitle('TableMate - Format tables');
  DocumentApp.getUi().showSidebar(ui);
}
</code></pre>
<p>If you change it like that, it should work.</p>

Q: How to reset radio button? A: <p>You should use the same key in your <code>setState</code>: <code>this.setState({ selectedDataValue: '' })</code>.</p>

<p>Also you only need to specify the changed keys in <code>setState</code>:</p>

<pre><code>this.setState({
  ...this.state, // this line can be removed
  selectedDataValue: event.target.value
});
</code></pre>

<p><strong>EDIT:</strong><br>
If you want to clear the radio selection, you can add in the <code>checked</code> prop: </p>

<pre><code>state = { ..., radioChecked: false };
...
&lt;input
  type="radio"
  checked={this.state.radioChecked}
  onClick={() =&gt; this.setState({ radioChecked: true })}
/&gt;
...
this.setState({ radioChecked: false }); // to clear it
</code></pre>

Q: no applicable method for &#39;group_by_&#39; applied to an object of class &quot;NULL&quot; in dplyr A: <p>Just add a function like this....</p>

<pre><code>if.is.empty &lt;- function(x){
    is.null(need(x, message = FALSE))}
</code></pre>

<p>and your codes looks like this....</p>

<pre><code>reg_city &lt;- function(){
    if (if.is.empty(final_data)) {
        final_data %&gt;% 
        group_by(registrant_city) %&gt;%
        summarise(Total= n()) %&gt;% 
        arrange(desc(Total)) %&gt;% 
        top_n(n=15)}
}
</code></pre>

<p>Note. Just be careful with the indentation...</p>

<p>This worked for me in a shiny app when it begins without info.</p>

Q: How to I pass parameters from ajax to web method? A: <p>You need to send an array from the <code>data</code> parameter in ajax. Try something like:</p>

<pre><code>var uval1 = $("#up_tb1").val();
var uval2 = $("#up_tb2").val();
function upbtnclicked() {
        alert('clicked');
        $.ajax({
            type: "POST",
            url: "WebForm1.aspx/updateData",
            data: {val1: uval1 ,val2: uval2 },
            contentType: "application/json; charset=utf-8",
            success: OnSuccess,
            error: OnErrorCall
        });

        function OnSuccess(response) {
            alert(response.d);
        }
        function OnErrorCall(response) { console.log(error); }
    }
</code></pre>
